WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.540
27 flight contacts are being traced after Kenya's first imported Ebola death. This is Omni

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:12.520
View Africa &amp; Middle East, episode 15. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.160
President William Ruto has told the National Security Council Committee to weigh extra steps

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.440
after that death. Capital FM reports through all Africa. The patient came from the Democratic Republic

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:30.780
of Congo, traveled through Uganda, and died Monday evening at the Nairobi hospital, two days after

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:37.240
admission to isolation. The hospital says the test showed Bundibugio Ebola, and the body has been

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:43.540
buried under public health rules. Chief Executive Felix Osano says the isolation unit is cut off from

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:49.340
the main building, with its own entrance and staff, and that the hospital is still open. He says

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.680
as simply working there or standing near the patient

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.700
is not automatically exposure.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.420
Statehouse spokesperson Hussein Muhammad

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.860
says that by October 6th,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.620
teams had screened 652,584 travelers

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.280
and tested 267 samples in five laboratories.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.360
Only this patient sample came back positive

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.640
and no further cases have been found.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.240
Eight relatives and 21 health workers

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.560
who treated the patient are in quarantine watched every day.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.700
identified contacts are followed with the Ministry of Health for 21 days. The

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:29.120
government says it has trained 4,971 health workers. Designated beds

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:34.360
stand at 8 at Kenyatta National Hospital, 50 at Moe Teaching and Referral Hospital,

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:41.080
49 at the National Police Hospital, and 143 at the Nairobi Hospital. Across the

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.640
region, Molly says its troops walked into Kedal on October 6 with Russia's

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.460
Africa Corps, taking back in northern city the army had left in April.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.720
Business Insider Africa reports the Azoad Liberation Front called the exit a strategic controlled

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.500
pullback, meant to keep its fighters intact under air pressure from Mollion forces and their

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.180
Russian partners.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:06.720
Two Mollion officers told AFP the column arrived early and met no resistance.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.800
Government spokesman Brigadier General Issa Usman Kulibali said air and ground units ran

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.760
the operation with Africa Corps help.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:20.540
Researcher Rita Lea Mori told the Associated Press the recapture is a major symbolic victory

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.700
for the central government.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:26.860
Africa Intelligence adds that the high command is formalizing links with militias already

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:31.600
fighting jihadist groups and their allies, and it describes heavy casualties around that

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.380
northern push.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:38.680
In Zimbabwe, President Emerson Manangagua has declared a state of disaster after Monday's

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:39.660
hailstorm in Moscow.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:46.820
Vingo. News in Bobley, carried by all Africa, says preliminary checks found about 8,500 households

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:53.080
with roofs completely torn off. 90% of 17,000 households assessed had shattered window

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:58.400
pains at the start of the rains. The damage list includes great Zimbabwe University's

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:05.060
Moucheque campus, Muzvingo Polytechnic, Muzvingo Teachers College, the Passport Office, Muzvingo

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:08.220
airport, and the maternity ward at Runya Raro Clinic.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.100
Zessa lines came down, and the blackout has hit water pumping,

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.700
drains, and sewers, which the report calls an immediate public health risk.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.100
Garway said the government had pulled in the resources it has,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.640
asked business and development partners to help,

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.740
and that assessments are still going while relief is sent out.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.000
Also today, in Accra, India's external affairs minister

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.760
S. Jai Shankar and Ghana's Sam Okudzeto Ablakwa

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:39.280
talked multilateral ties, including New Delhi's work with the African Union and ECOWAS,

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.440
and the sides exchanged memorandums on research and agricultural education.

